I take a cup of tea, it&#039;s too early and too grey.&lt;br /&gt;
So somber, so weak, what a horrible day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I put on my coat, hood over my head.&lt;br /&gt;
Damn this rain, I want to go back to bed.&lt;br /&gt;
I get in my car and start the tires.&lt;br /&gt;
Arrived at last, the caffeine expires.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I turn in my coat for a whiter one.&lt;br /&gt;
Must focus, procedure has begun.&lt;br /&gt;
Needed here to observe a test.&lt;br /&gt;
But I cannot help to feel stressed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Subject keeps getting stranger.&lt;br /&gt;
Don&#039;t provoke, D-class in danger.&lt;br /&gt;
Containment breached, stupid keter.&lt;br /&gt;
Results lost, all in the ether.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Got to control room, with little time bought.&lt;br /&gt;
Called for help, anomaly caught.&lt;br /&gt;
Explained to highers and senior.&lt;br /&gt;
No idea, why it&#039;s keener.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&#039;s murderous but in very bad shape.&lt;br /&gt;
How the hell did it manage to escape?&lt;br /&gt;
It can&#039;t leave site, security max degree.&lt;br /&gt;
But why do I think it&#039;s already free?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Going back home like the rest of the staff.&lt;br /&gt;
Can&#039;t help but to inner laugh.&lt;br /&gt;
Oh my, how they can&#039;t see…&lt;br /&gt;
That I&#039;m part of this SCP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Inspired by: A poem I wrote earlier for the wiki in basic AABB. Didn&#039;t post it because other things came up. I figured I could put it here instead of forgetting it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;span style=&quot;white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;&amp;#32;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-folded&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Used&amp;nbsp;formats&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded&quot; style=&quot;display:none&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-unfolded-link&quot;&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;collapsible-block-link&quot; href=&quot;javascript:;&quot;&gt;Close&amp;nbsp;formats&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;collapsible-block-content&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I did not necessarily stay true to these formats, but that also is the beauty of freedom poetry brings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kyrielle:&lt;/strong&gt; A French form in quatrains with 8 syllables per line that have AABB rhyme. Each quatrain must end with the same line. Fourth line gets repeated, all 3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; and 4&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt; lines rhyme.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Phantoum:&lt;/strong&gt; Quatrains where the second and fourth line become the first and the third line in the following quatrain. In the last quatrain the second and fourth line are the first and third of the first quatrain. Every line gets used twice. ABAB rhyme.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Limerick:&lt;/strong&gt; They only have 5 lines but they do count syllables and rhyme (AABBA). The most commonly known limericks are probably nursery rhymes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Butterfly:&lt;/strong&gt; 9 lines with 2-4-6-8-2-8-6-4-2 syllable count.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
